# Trading-proxy watchdog schedule: run every 2 minutes.
# Adjust the checkout path to the deployment.  Configuration comes from
# watchdog.env in the checkout root (see watchdog.env.example).
#
# */2 * * * *  $HOME/apps/Congress.Trade/scripts/ops/trading-proxy-watchdog/public-liveness-watch.sh
#
# Production today: the VM instance runs under the fleet scheduler with
# PUBLIC_FAIL_THRESHOLD=5, and a second instance on the home Mac runs
# under a LaunchAgent with PUBLIC_FAIL_THRESHOLD=8 and direct
# (no-egress-proxy) probing, so only a longer outage lets it restart.
